1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,621
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,624 --> 00:00:02,943
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,207 --> 00:00:05,207
(Episode 21)

4
00:00:25,192 --> 00:00:27,982
Dad, I did well, right?

5
00:00:28,865 --> 00:00:32,235
I didn't think about their side or ours.

6
00:00:34,265 --> 00:00:35,448
My bone marrow,

7
00:00:36,622 --> 00:00:38,968
please make sure, until the very end,

8
00:00:39,874 --> 00:00:42,059
that it gets successfully transplanted
to O Reum.

9
00:00:53,124 --> 00:00:55,110
(Director Im Ji Hu)

10
00:00:55,112 --> 00:00:56,197
Did you get home safely?

11
00:00:56,475 --> 00:00:58,790
Did your mother scold you for being late?

12
00:01:05,504 --> 00:01:07,358
(I'm sorry for sending you home late...)

13
00:01:11,172 --> 00:01:12,524
It was fine.

14
00:01:13,273 --> 00:01:15,107
Thank you for today.

15
00:01:15,814 --> 00:01:17,014
Please get some rest.

16
00:01:21,523 --> 00:01:23,896
(Do Hee)

17
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:26,797
Sorry I couldn't pick up earlier.

18
00:01:27,531 --> 00:01:30,171
- How's your father doing?
- Who were you with?

19
00:01:30,372 --> 00:01:32,370
Just someone.

20
00:01:33,132 --> 00:01:34,658
I asked how your father is doing.

21
00:01:35,005 --> 00:01:38,365
How many times are you going to ask?
He's fine.

22
00:01:38,792 --> 00:01:40,518
You should ask how I'm doing too.

23
00:01:40,911 --> 00:01:43,726
What I did today, how my mom is,

24
00:01:43,729 --> 00:01:46,290
how I'm feeling.

25
00:01:46,778 --> 00:01:47,792
Okay.

26
00:01:47,965 --> 00:01:49,132
How are you feeling?

27
00:01:49,945 --> 00:01:50,958
And your mom?

28
00:01:51,578 --> 00:01:53,660
Forcing it out of you is really fun.

29
00:01:53,912 --> 00:01:55,673
I went shopping with mom today.

30
00:01:55,965 --> 00:01:58,781
Check my Instagram,
I filled it with brand-new stuff.

31
00:01:58,925 --> 00:02:01,045
This isn't something money alone can buy,
you know.

32
00:02:01,252 --> 00:02:03,209
You need taste and the right environment.

33
00:02:03,923 --> 00:02:05,598
Yeah, I see.

34
00:02:06,838 --> 00:02:09,115
I'm glad your mom's feeling better.

35
00:02:10,194 --> 00:02:11,211
Okay.

36
00:02:12,152 --> 00:02:14,205
I'll call you later. Get some rest.

37
00:02:18,398 --> 00:02:19,405
What?

38
00:02:25,625 --> 00:02:29,376
- You seem busy even without Do Hee here.
- Dad.

39
00:02:30,532 --> 00:02:32,802
Are you getting the hang of things
at the center now?

40
00:02:33,272 --> 00:02:35,931
You started out pretty ambitiously,
even selling paintings.

41
00:02:35,933 --> 00:02:37,611
You heard from Mr. Il Dong, didn't you?

42
00:02:38,765 --> 00:02:40,262
They barely sold.

43
00:02:40,945 --> 00:02:42,625
Even our CEO is really disappointed.

44
00:02:42,627 --> 00:02:44,245
Selling paintings isn't easy.

45
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:45,750
People only see them as investments.

46
00:02:46,192 --> 00:02:47,398
I guess I was mistaken.

47
00:02:47,492 --> 00:02:48,616
Should I buy some?

48
00:02:48,972 --> 00:02:50,884
I could hang them in our newly expanded
publishing office.

49
00:02:52,112 --> 00:02:54,462
You sound like when you offered
to buy me a robot when I was nine.

50
00:02:54,464 --> 00:02:55,474
Did I?

51
00:02:55,995 --> 00:02:56,998
It's okay.

52
00:02:57,625 --> 00:03:00,368
I should accept that this one failed.

53
00:03:01,032 --> 00:03:03,378
The market for buying art here
isn't like it is overseas.

54
00:03:04,205 --> 00:03:05,211
I guess that's true.

55
00:03:05,885 --> 00:03:07,070
So that's why you came?

56
00:03:07,565 --> 00:03:08,825
I thought I'd buy a few paintings.

57
00:03:09,958 --> 00:03:11,671
I'll just take the loss this time.

58
00:03:12,512 --> 00:03:13,518
Okay.

59
00:03:15,092 --> 00:03:17,239
Then handle it your way. Get some rest.

60
00:03:18,287 --> 00:03:19,318
Okay.

61
00:03:30,798 --> 00:03:32,132
That's my son.

62
00:03:32,768 --> 00:03:34,176
What do you mean?

63
00:03:34,544 --> 00:03:35,643
Ji Hu.

64
00:03:35,792 --> 00:03:37,077
I heard the exhibition...

65
00:03:37,398 --> 00:03:39,476
got a good response,
but sales weren't great.

66
00:03:40,972 --> 00:03:43,840
Is it possible to have a good response
but low sales?

67
00:03:43,842 --> 00:03:44,858
Of course.

68
00:03:45,132 --> 00:03:48,388
People here think art collecting
is for a certain kind of crowd.

69
00:03:48,737 --> 00:03:50,944
Even in our house,
we rotate pieces from galleries, right?

70
00:03:50,952 --> 00:03:53,321
Still, if something's good, we keep it.

71
00:03:53,362 --> 00:03:55,063
- And invest in it.
- Exactly.

72
00:03:55,065 --> 00:03:56,388
It's about proving their investment value.

73
00:03:56,865 --> 00:03:58,578
Paintings need to prove their worth
as investments.

74
00:03:59,152 --> 00:04:01,605
Ji Hu probably thought
they'd sell as they do in Europe.

75
00:04:01,725 --> 00:04:04,950
Then why don't you buy some?
The kid's discouraged.

76
00:04:04,952 --> 00:04:06,648
I went to his room to do that,
but he refused.

77
00:04:07,312 --> 00:04:10,308
He needs to adapt to this environment
and come up with better, more solid plans.

78
00:04:10,382 --> 00:04:12,906
Then buy them secretly,
without him knowing.

79
00:04:13,061 --> 00:04:14,725
- "Secretly?"
- Yes.

80
00:04:15,011 --> 00:04:17,098
This is when parents should help.

81
00:04:18,405 --> 00:04:20,784
Have you ever hidden something
from me too?

82
00:04:21,052 --> 00:04:22,592
When have I ever done that?

83
00:04:24,732 --> 00:04:26,773
Let's respect Ji Hu's independence.

84
00:04:27,705 --> 00:04:29,961
He should experience failure and success.

85
00:04:30,132 --> 00:04:32,671
A man's life isn't all smooth sailing.

86
00:04:47,498 --> 00:04:49,534
Sa Bin, good morning.

87
00:04:49,536 --> 00:04:51,574
Did you sleep well, Sun Kyung?

88
00:04:52,191 --> 00:04:54,740
- Want me to pour it for you?
- Thank you.

89
00:04:57,012 --> 00:04:58,231
There are...

90
00:04:58,474 --> 00:05:00,511
a few shops in the building
that need lease renewals.

91
00:05:00,558 --> 00:05:03,085
It's been over ten years anyway,
so we'll redo them.

92
00:05:03,172 --> 00:05:04,701
Some places need repairs too.

93
00:05:05,281 --> 00:05:07,274
Okay, please handle it.

94
00:05:09,768 --> 00:05:12,636
- Is it hard for you?
- Then would you like to do it yourself?

95
00:05:12,638 --> 00:05:13,986
If that's the case, I will.

96
00:05:14,794 --> 00:05:15,972
Never mind.

97
00:05:16,018 --> 00:05:18,540
If you handle it,
you won't be able to raise the rent.

98
00:05:19,414 --> 00:05:21,361
Did you sleep well?

99
00:05:21,363 --> 00:05:23,285
I hate that greeting the most.

100
00:05:23,505 --> 00:05:24,794
So you didn't sleep again, did you?

101
00:05:25,412 --> 00:05:27,524
- What's for breakfast?
- Mallow soup.

102
00:05:28,257 --> 00:05:29,311
Okay.

103
00:05:37,632 --> 00:05:41,779
You're well fed and carefree,
no wonder you can't sleep.

104
00:05:44,565 --> 00:05:46,858
I said I don't care whether she was born
into this family or not,

105
00:05:47,565 --> 00:05:49,420
as long as the bone marrow matches.

106
00:05:49,558 --> 00:05:51,654
I get that, but...

107
00:05:51,902 --> 00:05:54,576
- how can you ask mom to go again?
- Why not?

108
00:05:54,872 --> 00:05:56,458
Is now the time to worry about pride?

109
00:05:56,518 --> 00:05:59,939
I'm willing to beg on my knees.
Why are you stopping me?

110
00:06:01,549 --> 00:06:03,027
That's just too much.

111
00:06:03,365 --> 00:06:05,470
Mai, it's not too much, it's...

112
00:06:05,472 --> 00:06:06,693
Then what is it?

113
00:06:07,098 --> 00:06:08,098
Are you even trying right now?

114
00:06:08,125 --> 00:06:10,322
Every minute that passes,
it's eating me alive.

115
00:06:10,325 --> 00:06:11,483
But all you say is...

116
00:06:11,616 --> 00:06:13,818
"Let's stay hopeful" and "Let's wait."

117
00:06:14,372 --> 00:06:15,418
If you were in my place,
could you do that?

118
00:06:21,858 --> 00:06:25,994
<i>Round and round, chubby chubby</i>

119
00:06:26,309 --> 00:06:30,205
<i>Round and round, chubby chubby</i>

120
00:06:30,207 --> 00:06:33,092
Grandma, you've got the lyrics wrong.

121
00:06:33,418 --> 00:06:36,134
<i>Round and round, chubby chubby</i>

122
00:06:36,293 --> 00:06:38,755
<i>Sing it with me</i>

123
00:06:39,593 --> 00:06:41,533
I see.

124
00:06:42,198 --> 00:06:44,965
My baby, you're so clever.

125
00:06:44,967 --> 00:06:47,285
Am I your baby?

126
00:06:48,325 --> 00:06:51,105
Of course you are.

127
00:06:57,671 --> 00:06:59,670
Okay, let's sleep, my dear O Reum.

128
00:07:01,525 --> 00:07:02,679
So pretty.

129
00:07:02,973 --> 00:07:04,118
Lie down like this.

130
00:07:04,952 --> 00:07:07,411
That's right, getting sleepy?

131
00:07:07,585 --> 00:07:08,748
My dear O Reum.

132
00:07:32,832 --> 00:07:34,410
I'll see O Reum before I head to work.

133
00:07:35,312 --> 00:07:37,338
I'll come straight back after,
so until then...

134
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:40,338
Don't worry, I'll take care of everything.

135
00:07:40,472 --> 00:07:43,360
I'll make sure mom
and Mai eat something too.

136
00:07:43,811 --> 00:07:46,617
This is exactly why
I ended up unemployed, you know?

137
00:07:47,579 --> 00:07:48,585
Thanks.

138
00:07:48,587 --> 00:07:49,602
Seung Hyun,

139
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:52,795
- try not to look so tense.
- I will, when I can.

140
00:07:52,836 --> 00:07:54,639
- I'm heading out.
- Seung Hyun.

141
00:07:55,631 --> 00:07:56,651
What?

142
00:07:58,904 --> 00:07:59,922
This might...

143
00:08:00,549 --> 00:08:01,650
sound harsh, but...

144
00:08:02,219 --> 00:08:03,339
just in case...

145
00:08:04,555 --> 00:08:05,918
I mean, in the worst-case scenario...

146
00:08:06,392 --> 00:08:07,658
What are you trying to say?

147
00:08:09,671 --> 00:08:12,031
You can always have another child.

148
00:08:12,355 --> 00:08:13,454
What on earth are you saying?

149
00:08:15,572 --> 00:08:17,449
Please don't misunderstand me.

150
00:08:17,972 --> 00:08:19,649
I'm not saying we should give up,

151
00:08:19,762 --> 00:08:21,511
or that it's not as important.

152
00:08:21,858 --> 00:08:22,871
But...

153
00:08:23,319 --> 00:08:24,531
Because of this,

154
00:08:24,534 --> 00:08:26,320
pushing mom this hard...

155
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:29,344
feels cruel to me.

156
00:08:33,811 --> 00:08:34,974
Think about it.

157
00:08:35,444 --> 00:08:37,008
Mom spent 30 years like that.

158
00:08:37,218 --> 00:08:39,441
She raised us like a widow,
even though she wasn't one.

159
00:08:41,525 --> 00:08:43,269
You were like a husband to her.

160
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:45,926
Do you really want to do this?

161
00:08:46,005 --> 00:08:47,738
Those 30 years are already over.

162
00:08:48,258 --> 00:08:49,391
I don't think it's too much to ask.

163
00:08:49,393 --> 00:08:51,245
- Seung Hyun.
- Don't say another word.

164
00:08:51,452 --> 00:08:52,604
I don't want to hear it.

165
00:08:54,549 --> 00:08:56,263
Seung Hyun.

166
00:08:58,264 --> 00:08:59,278
Mai.

167
00:09:02,858 --> 00:09:04,438
- Mai.
- Shut your mouth!

168
00:09:06,485 --> 00:09:07,561
I'm sorry...

169
00:09:11,331 --> 00:09:13,263
for giving birth to a sick child,

170
00:09:14,152 --> 00:09:15,171
I'm sorry.

171
00:09:21,212 --> 00:09:22,341
Don't say that.

172
00:09:22,929 --> 00:09:24,054
Even if the worst happens,

173
00:09:26,805 --> 00:09:28,088
and we lose O Reum,

174
00:09:28,380 --> 00:09:29,977
you must never say that.

175
00:09:31,368 --> 00:09:32,592
I was happy.

176
00:09:36,058 --> 00:09:38,197
Why are you saying that in the past tense?

177
00:10:03,238 --> 00:10:04,260
I'm here.

178
00:10:04,754 --> 00:10:05,818
Okay.

179
00:10:16,245 --> 00:10:17,459
Have you thought about it?

180
00:10:17,765 --> 00:10:18,811
What?

181
00:10:21,258 --> 00:10:23,037
- Are you seriously...
- No.

182
00:10:24,471 --> 00:10:27,538
- Don't do it if you're uncomfortable.
- What's wrong with you?

183
00:10:27,738 --> 00:10:30,406
There's no guarantee it'll match.
Why take it this far?

184
00:10:30,409 --> 00:10:32,425
I want to at least confirm
that it doesn't match.

185
00:10:32,475 --> 00:10:34,115
I already went there.

186
00:10:34,332 --> 00:10:35,471
To that house.

187
00:10:36,169 --> 00:10:39,128
The house full of photos
of your dad and that woman.

188
00:10:39,131 --> 00:10:41,616
I went there and begged them.

189
00:10:41,757 --> 00:10:42,982
They refused.

190
00:10:43,172 --> 00:10:44,504
And you want me to go again?

191
00:10:45,092 --> 00:10:47,598
Are my 30 years worth less
than your child?

192
00:10:50,325 --> 00:10:51,517
I understand.

193
00:11:01,398 --> 00:11:02,673
You brat.

194
00:11:03,025 --> 00:11:04,695
How can you only think about your child?

195
00:11:04,698 --> 00:11:07,151
How can you not see how your mother feels?

196
00:11:20,518 --> 00:11:21,651
O Reum.

197
00:11:23,898 --> 00:11:25,595
Dad is a bad son.

198
00:11:27,465 --> 00:11:29,172
Get well soon,

199
00:11:31,358 --> 00:11:33,120
and give your dad a scolding.

200
00:11:35,172 --> 00:11:37,479
Scold me...

201
00:11:39,798 --> 00:11:41,658
for hurting Grandma.

202
00:11:43,675 --> 00:11:45,210
Dad, are you crying?

203
00:11:48,905 --> 00:11:50,012
I'm sorry.

204
00:11:51,231 --> 00:11:52,822
Did I wake you up?

205
00:11:53,785 --> 00:11:57,065
Grandma's crying, and you're crying too.

206
00:11:58,245 --> 00:11:59,377
I'm sorry.

207
00:11:59,691 --> 00:12:01,254
Go back to sleep.

208
00:12:32,005 --> 00:12:33,204
What's the matter?

209
00:12:33,954 --> 00:12:36,326
Did you really come looking for me?

210
00:12:36,576 --> 00:12:38,149
Yes. You.

211
00:12:39,332 --> 00:12:40,816
I came for you, Na Ji Ni.

212
00:12:41,177 --> 00:12:42,190
Why?

213
00:12:43,325 --> 00:12:44,332
Let's go.

214
00:12:45,231 --> 00:12:48,181
Let's go get you tested.

215
00:12:48,538 --> 00:12:51,668
Just confirm that you
and O Reum aren't a match!

216
00:12:52,050 --> 00:12:53,535
You wicked girl.

217
00:12:56,132 --> 00:12:57,740
Why would I have to do that?

218
00:12:58,098 --> 00:12:59,306
Because of you,

219
00:12:59,928 --> 00:13:01,678
our family is breaking again.

220
00:13:01,992 --> 00:13:03,842
You know you broke it once before, right?

221
00:13:03,845 --> 00:13:05,016
And now,

222
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:06,694
because there's a chance...

223
00:13:06,696 --> 00:13:09,473
you might be a match,
we're falling apart every day.

224
00:13:10,292 --> 00:13:12,787
Mom and my brother are both falling apart.

225
00:13:14,472 --> 00:13:15,474
Who on earth...

226
00:13:15,842 --> 00:13:17,257
do you think you are,

227
00:13:17,870 --> 00:13:19,721
destroying our family twice?

228
00:13:20,889 --> 00:13:22,151
That's too bad.

229
00:13:26,125 --> 00:13:27,397
I'm begging you.

230
00:13:28,865 --> 00:13:30,602
O Reum is suffering so much.

231
00:13:31,918 --> 00:13:33,115
If you saw him,

232
00:13:33,449 --> 00:13:34,925
you couldn't refuse like this.

233
00:13:34,965 --> 00:13:36,535
That's why I won't go.

234
00:13:37,268 --> 00:13:38,305
So I don't have to see him.

235
00:13:41,638 --> 00:13:43,716
Could you talk to your mom...

236
00:13:44,538 --> 00:13:46,242
and take the test?

237
00:13:47,591 --> 00:13:49,130
Please.

238
00:13:58,558 --> 00:13:59,708
You know.

239
00:14:01,151 --> 00:14:02,504
I can't get on my knees.

240
00:14:04,018 --> 00:14:06,176
But in my heart, I'm already on my knees.

241
00:14:08,951 --> 00:14:10,210
I'm begging you.

242
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:37,592
- Hello.
- Yes, hello.

243
00:14:37,973 --> 00:14:39,792
You must be very busy.

244
00:14:39,992 --> 00:14:43,678
- I called, but you didn't answer.
- Did you?

245
00:14:44,169 --> 00:14:45,933
Sorry, but who are you?

246
00:14:46,186 --> 00:14:47,636
I'm the landlord here.

247
00:14:48,371 --> 00:14:51,156
You must have forgotten me
after all this time.

248
00:14:51,812 --> 00:14:54,212
I guess you didn't save my number either.

249
00:14:54,274 --> 00:14:57,780
Yes. How have you been?

250
00:14:57,845 --> 00:15:00,681
We're both busy, so I'll get to the point.

251
00:15:01,613 --> 00:15:04,249
You know the studio lease
is almost up, right?

252
00:15:04,493 --> 00:15:06,026
Already...

253
00:15:07,238 --> 00:15:09,504
Yes, you're right.

254
00:15:10,170 --> 00:15:14,964
This time, I'd like to raise the rent
and sign a new contract.

255
00:15:15,148 --> 00:15:16,725
About 30 percent?

256
00:15:17,252 --> 00:15:18,796
You've had this studio for a long time.

257
00:15:20,102 --> 00:15:21,504
Thirty percent?

258
00:15:21,596 --> 00:15:23,482
We'll be signing a new contract.

259
00:15:24,092 --> 00:15:26,612
The building exterior needs repainting,

260
00:15:26,615 --> 00:15:28,549
and many things need to be fixed.

261
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:33,128
If that doesn't work for you,
you can find another place.

262
00:15:34,262 --> 00:15:35,487
Okay...

263
00:15:36,565 --> 00:15:38,485
Then I'll leave it to you.

264
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:40,182
Okay.

265
00:15:55,410 --> 00:15:59,063
Because of you,
our family is breaking again.

266
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:01,085
You know you broke it once before, right?

267
00:16:01,129 --> 00:16:04,880
And now, because there's a chance
you might be a match,

268
00:16:04,883 --> 00:16:06,886
we're falling apart every day.

269
00:16:07,590 --> 00:16:09,904
Mom and my brother are both falling apart.

270
00:16:10,772 --> 00:16:13,560
Who on earth do you think you are,

271
00:16:13,921 --> 00:16:15,917
destroying our family twice?

272
00:16:27,887 --> 00:16:31,482
Doctor, aren't the results out yet?

273
00:16:31,652 --> 00:16:33,860
It must be hard for everyone waiting.

274
00:16:34,851 --> 00:16:37,741
Okay. I understand.

275
00:16:41,003 --> 00:16:43,446
Popcorn is a must for movies.

276
00:16:45,125 --> 00:16:48,056
We're only going to watch this for work.
Aren't you having too much fun?

277
00:16:48,577 --> 00:16:50,249
Working while having fun...

278
00:16:50,629 --> 00:16:51,921
is the best, isn't it?

279
00:16:53,807 --> 00:16:55,053
Who is it?

280
00:16:56,468 --> 00:16:59,164
- Jung A again?
- Yeah, Jung A again.

281
00:17:00,455 --> 00:17:02,742
Yeah, Jung A again.
Why do you keep calling?

282
00:17:03,049 --> 00:17:05,475
What? The landlady?

283
00:17:06,826 --> 00:17:09,296
She says they're raising the rent
for the whole building.

284
00:17:09,379 --> 00:17:11,255
- Your studio too.
- Really?

285
00:17:11,318 --> 00:17:13,347
I haven't even received
my first paycheck yet.

286
00:17:14,198 --> 00:17:16,128
Okay, I got it.

287
00:17:16,131 --> 00:17:18,501
We'll figure it out. Okay.

288
00:17:20,253 --> 00:17:22,649
Well, it has been a long time.

289
00:17:22,652 --> 00:17:26,556
My sister had it for five years,
then I took it over for six years.

290
00:17:27,150 --> 00:17:28,802
- What about you?
- It's been three years.

291
00:17:28,805 --> 00:17:30,687
Then you should be fine.

292
00:17:30,690 --> 00:17:34,379
But aren't you from a rich family?
Why are you worried?

293
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:36,702
I didn't earn that money.
It's not mine to spend as I please.

294
00:17:37,843 --> 00:17:42,860
If you're not independent by 30,
no one treats you well.

295
00:17:43,210 --> 00:17:46,371
Jung A said she's going
to your home tonight.

296
00:17:46,687 --> 00:17:47,921
I know.

297
00:17:49,292 --> 00:17:52,938
I'm not in the mood for a movie,
but work is work.

298
00:17:53,693 --> 00:17:54,813
Let's do this!

299
00:18:24,379 --> 00:18:25,829
That's quite a sigh.

300
00:18:25,832 --> 00:18:28,484
The landlord raised the rent
right after I took over.

301
00:18:28,652 --> 00:18:29,972
Can you believe my luck?

302
00:18:30,034 --> 00:18:31,449
Your business is doing well.

303
00:18:31,530 --> 00:18:35,057
Another café just opened next door.
That's the problem.

304
00:18:36,721 --> 00:18:39,521
So why did your mom say
we couldn't come out?

305
00:18:42,156 --> 00:18:45,885
- Girls, come here.
- Yes, Ma'am.

306
00:18:51,521 --> 00:18:52,817
Well?

307
00:18:53,116 --> 00:18:55,585
You look gorgeous!

308
00:18:56,127 --> 00:18:58,541
- Really?
- What's the occasion?

309
00:18:58,544 --> 00:19:01,497
I'm going to Indonesia on a business trip.

310
00:19:02,068 --> 00:19:04,684
I'm checking out
the company he invested in...

311
00:19:04,686 --> 00:19:07,039
to decide whether to keep investing.

312
00:19:07,052 --> 00:19:09,350
- Like you'd know what to look for.
- You brat.

313
00:19:09,411 --> 00:19:11,345
The attorney's coming with me.

314
00:19:11,348 --> 00:19:13,617
Besides, I've learned a lot.

315
00:19:13,853 --> 00:19:16,633
- Less talking. Help me pick an outfit.
- You're taking all these?

316
00:19:16,636 --> 00:19:20,130
No, I'll only be there for a few days,
but there are two parties.

317
00:19:20,194 --> 00:19:23,666
And I need an airport outfit too.

318
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:25,095
Who's going to see you?

319
00:19:25,154 --> 00:19:26,800
Do I need an audience?

320
00:19:27,247 --> 00:19:31,133
- The best cure for a bad mood is...
- Fashion.

321
00:19:32,102 --> 00:19:34,165
Jung A gets it.

322
00:19:35,310 --> 00:19:38,668
Ma'am, you should be a senior model.
You'd be amazing.

323
00:19:39,613 --> 00:19:42,923
People do tell me that.

324
00:19:43,798 --> 00:19:47,234
Just be careful. Don't celebrate too soon.

325
00:19:47,369 --> 00:19:49,875
You spent your whole life
focused on sheet music.

326
00:19:49,877 --> 00:19:51,276
Sheet music never lies.

327
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,258
If you trust people
the way you trust sheet music...

328
00:19:53,916 --> 00:19:54,963
I know.

329
00:19:54,977 --> 00:19:57,987
Yeah. You nag like an old lady.

330
00:19:57,990 --> 00:19:59,981
I'm sure she knows what she's doing.

331
00:20:00,932 --> 00:20:03,447
Ma'am, try this on.

332
00:20:03,626 --> 00:20:04,860
Should I?

333
00:20:08,220 --> 00:20:09,356
How is it?

334
00:20:09,862 --> 00:20:11,499
It does look nice.

335
00:20:12,973 --> 00:20:15,752
- Wouldn't it look great in the wind?
- It looks amazing.

336
00:20:26,220 --> 00:20:27,840
Mother.

337
00:20:30,302 --> 00:20:32,129
I heard from Seung Hyun.

338
00:20:33,369 --> 00:20:35,207
His immune levels have dropped.

339
00:20:36,889 --> 00:20:38,300
Mother.

340
00:20:39,243 --> 00:20:41,786
We're not going to lose O Reum, right?

341
00:20:41,788 --> 00:20:42,965
Of course not.

342
00:20:43,830 --> 00:20:46,824
Don't even say that.
I don't want to think about it.

343
00:20:53,382 --> 00:20:55,272
You're going to collapse first.

344
00:20:55,769 --> 00:20:57,275
Let's eat something.

345
00:21:07,853 --> 00:21:10,470
At least drink some water. Come on.

346
00:22:02,721 --> 00:22:05,965
It must feel like visiting a grave.
Why do you keep coming?

347
00:22:07,723 --> 00:22:09,112
Yeong Ju, how do I look?

348
00:22:09,512 --> 00:22:11,889
I had a fitting because I'm going
on a business trip to Indonesia...

349
00:22:12,259 --> 00:22:13,493
Yeong Ju.

350
00:22:13,552 --> 00:22:15,272
What's wrong with you?

351
00:22:15,570 --> 00:22:18,653
Don't do this. Are you filming
some historical drama or something?

352
00:22:18,721 --> 00:22:20,712
Let's not do this.

353
00:22:21,932 --> 00:22:23,171
Honestly,

354
00:22:23,980 --> 00:22:25,874
I'm just that desperate.

355
00:22:26,434 --> 00:22:27,962
- Yeong Ju.
- Let me...

356
00:22:28,405 --> 00:22:29,904
speak first.

357
00:22:30,572 --> 00:22:32,705
I'm sorry for blaming you
for my husband's affair...

358
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:36,093
and for giving birth to Ji Ni.

359
00:22:37,184 --> 00:22:39,083
I'm sorry for turning her away...

360
00:22:39,125 --> 00:22:42,792
when she was young and begged me
to let her take the Cha family name.

361
00:22:45,452 --> 00:22:46,879
I said so many cruel things...

362
00:22:47,815 --> 00:22:49,571
to her when she was young.

363
00:22:50,068 --> 00:22:51,382
I admit it too.

364
00:22:57,690 --> 00:23:00,619
- She told us never to come out.
- You know that too.

365
00:23:01,050 --> 00:23:02,375
This isn't the time for this.

366
00:23:02,432 --> 00:23:05,680
But if you go out there now
and tell her it's over, not to worry,

367
00:23:06,055 --> 00:23:07,546
what would that make your mom?

368
00:23:08,287 --> 00:23:10,514
Absolutely not. It'll be a disaster.

369
00:23:11,365 --> 00:23:12,788
Just hold on a little longer.

370
00:23:14,612 --> 00:23:16,613
Once the tests are done,
he'll get the transplant, right?

371
00:23:18,881 --> 00:23:20,853
They said 24 hours.

372
00:23:21,718 --> 00:23:23,197
It'll happen soon.

373
00:23:24,695 --> 00:23:26,801
You really never know
what life has in store.

374
00:23:27,692 --> 00:23:28,962
You said you'd think...

375
00:23:29,798 --> 00:23:32,158
if I came and apologized...

376
00:23:32,683 --> 00:23:34,346
for insulting Ji Ni.

377
00:23:34,401 --> 00:23:35,879
Did they tell you that?

378
00:23:37,137 --> 00:23:38,207
Sons...

379
00:23:38,262 --> 00:23:39,839
Children are all the same.

380
00:23:40,847 --> 00:23:43,582
Especially after they
have a kid of their own.

381
00:23:46,172 --> 00:23:48,142
I'm not blaming him for that,

382
00:23:48,725 --> 00:23:50,542
and I understand why he did it.

383
00:23:51,572 --> 00:23:53,510
I came back and apologized, so...

384
00:23:55,629 --> 00:23:57,269
so please let her do this, Se Ri.

385
00:23:57,930 --> 00:23:59,313
You're right.

386
00:23:59,672 --> 00:24:01,301
If you hadn't given birth to her,

387
00:24:01,824 --> 00:24:03,373
would we even have this chance?

388
00:24:04,292 --> 00:24:05,935
Who would've thought...

389
00:24:05,942 --> 00:24:08,410
she'd become a glimmer of hope for O Reum?

390
00:24:09,572 --> 00:24:12,022
I'm truly sorry, and I'm grateful.

391
00:24:13,276 --> 00:24:15,146
Please, I'm really asking you.

392
00:24:17,395 --> 00:24:20,058
- There's one thing left.
- What?

393
00:24:21,990 --> 00:24:26,072
You still haven't apologized
for what really hurt me.

394
00:24:28,801 --> 00:24:30,017
Yeah.

395
00:24:34,358 --> 00:24:36,428
I'm sorry for taunting you,

396
00:24:37,895 --> 00:24:41,271
while holding onto those documents.

397
00:24:42,092 --> 00:24:43,534
Because of you,

398
00:24:43,537 --> 00:24:46,006
I couldn't even call Ji Ni my daughter,

399
00:24:46,203 --> 00:24:48,904
and suffered in silence
for over ten years.

400
00:24:49,403 --> 00:24:52,081
You think one apology makes up for that?

401
00:24:54,430 --> 00:24:56,790
Because of you, my daughter and I spent...

402
00:24:56,881 --> 00:24:58,857
those years trapped in a dark tunnel.

403
00:24:59,312 --> 00:25:01,622
That's why he couldn't leave us.

404
00:25:02,548 --> 00:25:04,188
Now you know what it's like
to have no light left in your life,

405
00:25:04,876 --> 00:25:09,821
and to feel yourself slowly dying inside
a little more with every passing day.

406
00:25:10,590 --> 00:25:12,490
These days,
you're the one in the tunnel, right?

407
00:25:13,777 --> 00:25:17,623
Now you know what it feels like
to have no light.

408
00:25:18,203 --> 00:25:20,166
Now you know what it's like...

409
00:25:20,169 --> 00:25:23,565
to watch your child suffer.

410
00:25:25,247 --> 00:25:28,006
Watching my daughter
get bullied by her friends,

411
00:25:28,177 --> 00:25:30,774
I felt like I was tearing
myself apart every day.

412
00:25:32,475 --> 00:25:33,697
But...

413
00:25:35,552 --> 00:25:37,295
you want to end it like this?

414
00:25:38,544 --> 00:25:41,263
I can't. I won't let her do it.

415
00:25:42,367 --> 00:25:44,983
Since Min Ki died,
my daughter and I have been at peace.

416
00:25:46,363 --> 00:25:51,882
What am I supposed to do now
for you to let her get tested?

417
00:25:52,540 --> 00:25:56,467
No, I can't. I won't. So leave!

418
00:25:56,624 --> 00:26:00,326
I don't care if that family's
grandson dies.

419
00:26:00,629 --> 00:26:02,272
You said the same thing to me, too.

420
00:26:02,274 --> 00:26:05,066
Se Ri, please.

421
00:26:05,104 --> 00:26:07,731
What if her bone marrow is a match?

422
00:26:08,012 --> 00:26:11,340
Then the whole family will come after us
and make our lives miserable.

423
00:26:11,605 --> 00:26:13,916
No. Absolutely not.

424
00:26:14,321 --> 00:26:15,728
Leave!

425
00:26:40,089 --> 00:26:42,163
Mrs. No.

426
00:26:45,710 --> 00:26:48,366
What's wrong?

427
00:26:49,137 --> 00:26:50,388
Were you crying?

428
00:26:50,746 --> 00:26:52,041
Why...

429
00:26:55,571 --> 00:26:59,390
It's not fair. I'm so angry.

430
00:27:00,691 --> 00:27:03,790
I even told her I was grateful...

431
00:27:04,249 --> 00:27:06,382
for having my husband's child.

432
00:27:06,965 --> 00:27:11,318
That bastard. How could he do this to me?

433
00:27:12,960 --> 00:27:16,052
I'm so angry. I'm losing my mind.

434
00:27:16,054 --> 00:27:20,316
But I can't even be angry
because of O Reum.

435
00:27:43,617 --> 00:27:47,639
That bastard.

436
00:28:23,130 --> 00:28:26,156
(Family Register)

437
00:28:26,241 --> 00:28:29,083
- Be upset only until today.
- Yes, only until today.

438
00:28:29,137 --> 00:28:30,300
You're an artist, right?

439
00:28:30,350 --> 00:28:32,910
- Is that really all you can do?
- What exactly is bothering you this time?

440
00:28:32,970 --> 00:28:35,264
How much do you love Do Hee?
The choice is yours.

441
00:28:35,318 --> 00:28:37,866
Now she wants my help? She has some nerve.

442
00:28:37,933 --> 00:28:39,857
I wanted to tell Sa Bin.

443
00:28:39,916 --> 00:28:41,706
Because you're the one
who comforted me so much.

444
00:28:41,748 --> 00:28:44,906
I won't pretend I don't know.
I'll tell you myself.

445
00:28:47,378 --> 00:28:49,378
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
